---
/**
 * Mutual signatures: each key attests ownership of the other → cross-network identity.
 */
---

<figure class="concept-diagram" aria-labelledby="mutual-bind-caption">
  <div
    class="mutual-bind"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Nostr key and Ethereum key each sign ownership of the other, forming one cross-network identity"
  >
    <div class="bind-key bind-key--nostr">
      <span class="bind-key-name">Nostr key</span>
      <span class="bind-key-hint">Communication identity</span>
    </div>

    <div class="bind-arrows" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg class="bind-arrows-svg" viewBox="0 0 120 80" width="120" height="80">
        <defs>
          <marker
            id="bind-arrowhead"
            markerWidth="8"
            markerHeight="8"
            refX="6"
            refY="4"
            orient="auto"
          >
            <path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 Z" fill="currentColor" />
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <path
          class="bind-arrow-top"
          d="M8 22 H100"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          marker-end="url(#bind-arrowhead)"
        />
        <text x="60" y="14" text-anchor="middle" class="bind-arrow-label">
          signs: I own this Ethereum key
        </text>
        <path
          class="bind-arrow-bottom"
          d="M112 58 H20"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          marker-end="url(#bind-arrowhead)"
        />
        <text x="60" y="74" text-anchor="middle" class="bind-arrow-label">
          signs: I own this Nostr key
        </text>
      </svg>
      <div class="bind-arrows-stack">
        <p class="bind-step">Nostr key signs: “I own this Ethereum key”</p>
        <p class="bind-step">Ethereum key signs: “I own this Nostr key”</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bind-key bind-key--eth">
      <span class="bind-key-name">Ethereum key</span>
      <span class="bind-key-hint">Governance identity</span>
    </div>

    <div class="bind-result">
      <span class="bind-result-label">Cross-network identity</span>
      <span class="bind-result-body">
        Private chat on Nostr · people, app, and assets governable on Ethereum
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="mutual-bind-caption" class="concept-diagram-caption">
    Signing means proving control of a key with cryptography — not a password you type into a
    website. Each key vouching for the other ties the two networks to one person.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
